A||||1||Frank R||Electrical Test  Real Easy||||6||
Z||000000||Frank R||04-25-2000||11:27 PM||||This little test is to determine if the battery has any unknown drains.  You may use a 12 volt trouble lite, an old headlite or any car horn to do this test.  Remove the grille over the battery.  Remove the battery's ground cable connection.  Connect any lite or horn to the battery's cable and the other test wire to the battery's negative post.  Now if there is any electrical activity, the horn will sound or the lite will come on.  Every electrical device will show when it is on.  The actual power user will not operate only the test device.  Some cars with a quarty clock and radio with memory must be unfused.  Open the door, the lite or horn will tell.  On occasions, all the fuses must be slowly removed until the battery eater is found.  When using a digital voltmeter, it should be noted that a fully charged battery will reflect 12.6 volts.  A battery with only 25% charge will show 12.0 volts....Frank R||||reg||6
